  "notes": "P2 pseudo-RAW (three collocated channels, no CFA phase) motion training arm, DEV SCALE. Same seeds, budget tier, validation interval, delta_val, schedule, optimizer and evaluation buckets as configs/encoders/n01_full/p2_motion_train.json (the cfa4 arm), so the two runs differ only by the stem input domain: synthetic CFA 4 phases (packed 2 sensor px per cell) vs rawvla_rgb3 three co-located channels (packed 1 sensor px per cell). The shipped pseudo_raw_geometry (128x128 sensor, channel_phase=[]) is used as-is and every pixel-valued recipe length is scaled by 2 to preserve the declared relative scene at that resolution. The authorised formal budget (three seeds x 100k) covers the cfa4 arm only; this arm is delivered at development scale (fit-check now, a 256-update dev run on the server) and its numbers are not a formal-budget result.",
